## Session Management

### Session Data Structure

```javascript
req.session = {
    userInfo: {
        email: "user@login.gov",
        IDP: "login.gov",       // 'nih', 'login.gov', or 'test-idp'
        firstName: "John",
        lastName: "Doe"
    },
    tokens: "<access_token>"    // OAuth access token from NIH
}
```

### Session Configuration

| Config Key | Purpose | Default |
|---|---|---|
| `SESSION_SECRET` | Cookie signing secret | (required, from environment) |
| `SESSION_TIMEOUT` | Session timeout in seconds | `1800` (30 minutes) |

### Session Lifecycle

| Event | Trigger | Effect |
|---|---|---|
| Creation | Successful `POST /login` | Session stored in MongoDB, `connect.sid` cookie sent |
| Refresh | `POST /authenticated` | Session TTL reset |
| Expiration | No activity for `SESSION_TIMEOUT` | Session auto-deleted by MongoDB TTL index |
| Destruction | `POST /logout` | Session deleted from MongoDB, cookie cleared |

### Session Cookie

- Cookie name: `connect.sid`
- Signed with `SESSION_SECRET`
- Stored server-side in MongoDB `sessions` collection
- Session ID extractable from cookie for TTL queries

