## Mapping to Katalon Test Automation

### How Auth Service Maps to Katalon Keywords

| Auth Service Operation | What Happens | Katalon Keyword |
|---|---|---|
| NIH OAuth authorize redirect | Browser navigates to NIH login page | `Login.navigateToCrdc()` starts the flow |
| Login.gov OTP entry | User enters credentials + OTP on Login.gov | `Login.loginToCrdcOtp(pbacUser)` automates this |
| `POST /api/authn/login` | Code exchange + session creation | Handled automatically by browser after OAuth redirect |
| `connect.sid` cookie set | Session persists across requests | Cookie maintained by Selenium WebDriver throughout test |
| `POST /api/authn/authenticated` | Session check/refresh | Called by UI periodically; relevant for session timeout tests |
| `POST /api/authn/logout` | Session destroyed | `SubmissionRequest.logoutFromCrdc()` triggers this |
| `GET /api/authn/session-ttl` | Check remaining session time | Useful for inactivity timeout testing |

### Login Keyword to Auth Service Mapping

The `Login.loginToCrdcOtp(pbacUser)` keyword automates the full OAuth flow:

1. Clicks "Continue" on the system use warning
2. Clicks the Login button
3. Clicks the Login.gov icon (triggers OAuth redirect to NIH SSO)
4. Enters email/password on Login.gov page
5. Generates and enters OTP via Python script (`PythonFiles/CRDC/GenerateOtp.py`)
6. Clicks Grant (OAuth consent)
7. Browser receives OAuth code, frontend calls `POST /api/authn/login`
8. Session cookie (`connect.sid`) is set automatically

The `pbacUser` parameter selects which test account credentials to use:

| pbacUser | Role | Maps to Auth Service |
|---|---|---|
| `'Admin'` | Admin | `isEmailAndIDPLoginPermitted` must pass for admin email |
| `'Fedlead'` | Federal Lead | Same check for fedlead email |
| `'Dcp'` | Data Commons Personnel | Same check for DCP email |
| `'Submitter'` | Submitter | Same check for submitter email |
| `'User'` | User | Same check for user email |

### Understanding Auth for Test Design

When designing auth-related tests:

1. **Session timeout tests**: The auth service session timeout is configurable via `SESSION_TIMEOUT` (default 30 min). The UI shows an inactivity dialog before timeout. The `/api/authn/session-ttl` endpoint returns remaining seconds.
2. **User status tests**: Setting a user to `INACTIVE` in the database will cause `POST /api/authn/login` to return 403. Useful for testing disabled user scenarios.
3. **Multi-IDP testing**: Users authenticating via NIH vs Login.gov follow the same OAuth flow but get different IDP values stored in their session.
4. **Session persistence**: All Selenium requests carry the `connect.sid` cookie automatically. No special handling needed in Katalon unless testing cross-browser or incognito scenarios.
5. **Logout verification**: After `POST /api/authn/logout`, the session is destroyed server-side. Verify by checking that `POST /api/authn/authenticated` returns `{status: false}`.

